comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-15T10:41:12.886Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence 2026-08-15: all-status searches for contracts --json --full,omitted_result,requested_budget_infeasible,JSON.parse,and GitHub #1030 found no item for this current command-path regression. Open parent pm-5t33or owns the universal budget contract; closed pm-8nev0o,pm-jt8aa2,pm-x0iv17,and pm-s2h0mq provide completed resumability,omission-receipt,full-projection,and default-ceiling lineage. This issue records the newly reproduced cross-surface gap without reopening or duplicating those items."
  "2026-08-15T10:41:57.903Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage and live reproduction evidence 2026-08-15: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1030#issuecomment-5301862505 points GitHub #1030 to this canonical PM item. On repository main 996313a99, the bounded invocation returned only output_budget_exceeded/read_output with omitted_result=true; the unbounded control returned 26 top-level keys, 131 commands, and 104 actions."
body: "## Verified live evidence\n\nAt main 996313a99bf7df942111cac40b8ada53107dcfe5:\n\n- pm contracts --json --full returns only output_budget_exceeded and read_output.\n- output_budget_exceeded.omitted_result is true and reason is requested_budget_infeasible.\n- pm --output-budget unbounded contracts --json --full returns 26 top-level keys, 131 commands, and 104 actions.\n\n## Contract decision required\n\nThe implementation must distinguish three cases:\n\n1. explicit complete-result intent with no explicit budget: completeness wins;\n2. explicit caller budget: the caller's cost ceiling wins and any omission is disclosed;\n3. whole-result omission: this is a failed read, not a successful bounded projection, and must not be parseable as plausible domain data.\n\nThis rule belongs in the shared SDK read-output primitive, not as a contracts-only bypass.\n\n## Regression lineage\n\nGH-1012 and the closed resumability lineage fixed complete-result handling on list-all. The same semantic class now appears on contracts --full, proving the behavior needs a cross-surface invariant."
